Repo: monokl (AGENTS.md and CLAUDE.md apply; read AGENTS.md Non-negotiables, Testing and "A change is done when"). Quirks: use /usr/bin/git, one plain git command per call (no pipes, compound commands or -C); cargo, git commit and git push need the sandbox disabled; one cargo command at a time; macOS sed needs `-i ""`.

Task: PR 68 (branch `feat/member-blocks-object-literals`, object-literal member rows, stacked on `feat/member-blocks-class-methods` = PR 66) needs a fix-up. Do this on that existing branch: `git fetch origin`, `git switch --detach origin/feat/member-blocks-object-literals`, then `git merge origin/feat/member-blocks-class-methods` (PR 66 just gained commit d9a6c28 changing `owned_hits` in crates/monokl/src/pipeline/mod.rs to decide ownership by the text each block holds on a line; resolve conflicts keeping both sides' intent). Push with `git push origin HEAD:feat/member-blocks-object-literals` (never force). Do not open a new PR or trail.

An adversarial review of PR 68 found these, all reproduced against the old line-granular ownership; PR 66's fix addresses the root cause for classes and your merge brings it in. Add object-literal tests (crates/monokl/tests/members.rs style: tempdir project, exact-value asserts, written so they FAIL on a build without the ownership fix; prove it by temporarily reverting only the owned_hits change, running them, then restoring):
1. Sibling members sharing a line: `const o = { a() {
  return needleX;
}, b() {
  return needleY;
} };` with query `regex:b\(\)` must return only b's block with matched line 3 (before: a also got line 3 and a spurious row with snippet `3: }`).
2. Header-line match: same file, query `const` must keep the holder `o` row with matched line 1 (before: the member took the line, the holder was dropped, the member row showed nothing that matched).
3. Trailing comment: `export const svc = {
  load() {
    return 1;
  }, // zebra note
  save() {
    return 2;
  },
};` with query `zebra` must give the holder the line (before: the row for load() showed snippet `}`).
Also fix these low findings: (a) the empty-result hint in crates/monokl/src/output/agent.rs says "only top-level declarations and class members are searched" but object-literal members are searched too; reword it truthfully (keep it short) and update the test in crates/monokl/tests/cli.rs and any README text that quotes it; (b) rustdoc of `search()` in pipeline/mod.rs and of `ParentContext` in types.rs name only classes; say classes and object literals; (c) the tests the reviewer showed pass without the change (`only_the_full_profile_extracts_object_member_blocks` and the 13-case negative rstest assert zero blocks, which was already true; `no_line_of_an_object_is_credited_to_two_blocks_whatever_the_query` uses a fixture with no shared line): keep the negative tests only if they pin a real rule, otherwise delete them, and make the no-double-credit test use a fixture with a shared line so it can fail. Leave `module.exports = {}` and nested objects as documented gaps.

Run `just lint`, `just test`, `just doc-check`, `just deny`, `just machete`, `just check-drift`, `just changesets`, `just coverage`, and `python3 -I scripts/rg-compare.py` (identifier hit@3 56/59, declaration_in_output all, questions 14/18 must not drop). Commits: Conventional Commits, no hard wraps, end each message with the line `Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AdtWVgDi4y4qCnpfdozb2n`. Final report at most 200 words: what you pushed, the commit hashes, which new tests failed without the fix, and the real numbers from the commands you ran.

